      0.819,
      0.169
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "The new elements are written \\( a_{rc}^{(2)} \\) to indicate that this is the second time that a number has been stored in the matrix at location \\( (r, c) \\). The result after step 2 is",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.307,
      0.177,
      0.652,
      0.322
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{c c c c c c} a _ {1 1} ^ {(1)} & a _ {1 2} ^ {(1)} & a _ {1 3} ^ {(1)} & \\dots & a _ {1 N} ^ {(1)} & a _ {1 N + 1} ^ {(1)} \\\\ 0 & a _ {2 2} ^ {(2)} & a _ {2 3} ^ {(2)} & \\dots & a _ {2 N} ^ {(2)} & a _ {2 N + 1} ^ {(2)} \\\\ 0 & a _ {3 2} ^ {(2)} & a _ {3 3} ^ {(2)} & \\dots & a _ {3 N} ^ {(2)} & a _ {3 N + 1} ^ {(2)} \\\\ \\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & & \\vdots & \\vdots \\\\ 0 & a _ {N 2} ^ {(2)} & a _ {N 3} ^ {(2)} & \\dots & a _ {N N} ^ {(2)} & a _ {N N + 1} ^ {(2)} \\end{array} \\right]\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.149,
      0.329,
      0.82,
      0.379
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "Step 3. If necessary, switch the second row with some row below it so that \\( a_{22}^{(2)} \\neq 0 \\); then eliminate \\( x_{2} \\) in rows 3 through \\( N \\). In this process, \\( m_{r2} \\) is the multiple of row 2 that is subtracted from row \\( r \\).",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.348,
      0.389,
      0.586,
      0.512
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\n\\begin{array}{l} \\text { for } r = 3: N \\\\ m _ {r 2} = a _ {r 2} ^ {(2)} / a _ {2 2} ^ {(2)}; \\\\ a _ {r 2} ^ {(3)} = 0; \\\\ \\text {for} c = 3: N + 1 \\\\ a _ {r c} ^ {(3)} = a _ {r c} ^ {(2)} \\quad m _ {r 2} * a _ {2 c} ^ {(2)}; \\\\ \\text {end} \\\\ \\end{array}\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.351,
      0.499,
      0.383,
      0.511
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "end",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.15,
      0.525,
      0.82,
      0.562
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "The new elements are written \\( a_{rc}^{(3)} \\) to indicate that this is the third time that a number has been stored in the matrix at location \\( (r, c) \\). The result after step 3 is",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.31,
      0.569,
      0.655,
      0.715
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\n\\left[ \\begin{array}{c c c c c c} a _ {1 1} ^ {(1)} & a _ {1 2} ^ {(1)} & a _ {1 3} ^ {(1)} & \\dots & a _ {1 N} ^ {(1)} & a _ {1 N + 1} ^ {(1)} \\\\ 0 & a _ {2 2} ^ {(2)} & a _ {2 3} ^ {(2)} & \\dots & a _ {2 N} ^ {(2)} & a _ {2 N + 1} ^ {(2)} \\\\ 0 & 0 & a _ {3 3} ^ {(3)} & \\dots & a _ {3 N} ^ {(3)} & a _ {3 N + 1} ^ {(3)} \\\\ \\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & & \\vdots & \\vdots \\\\ 0 & 0 & a _ {N 3} ^ {(3)} & \\dots & a _ {N N} ^ {(3)} & a _ {N N + 1} ^ {(3)} \\end{array} \\right]\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.151,
      0.722,
      0.823,
      0.773
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "Step \\( p + 1 \\). This is the general step. If necessary, switch row \\( p \\) with some row beneath it so that \\( a_{pp}^{(p)} \\neq 0 \\); then eliminate \\( x_p \\) in rows \\( p + 1 \\) through \\( N \\). Here \\( m_{rp} \\) is the multiple of row \\( p \\) that is subtracted from row \\( r \\).",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.35,
      0.782,
      0.512,
      0.841
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\n\\begin{array}{l} \\text { for } r = p + 1: N \\\\ m _ {r p} = a _ {r p} ^ {(p)} / a _ {p p} ^ {(p)}; \\\\ a _ {r p} ^ {(p + 1)} = 0; \\\\ \\end{array}\n\\]"
  }
